<title>POLAND: POLISH NET RESERVES FALL TO $21.29 BLN IN JAN 1-20.</title>
<headline>POLISH NET RESERVES FALL TO $21.29 BLN IN JAN 1-20.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish net foreign currency</p>
<p>reserves fell by $374.2 million in January 1-20 to $21.29</p>
<p>billion, the National Bank of Poland said.</p>
<p>    POLISH RESERVES (bln dlrs)  JAN 1-20  DEC 96	JAN 96</p>
<p>    Net reserves		     21.29    21.67(21.81) 21.44</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures in billions of dollars. Official reserves</p>
<p>are those held by the state. Net reserves mean the total amount</p>
<p>of hard currencies in the whole banking system. Revised figures</p>
<p>in brackets.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
